<title>GREECE: TRIENA, ASPIS LEAD GREEK MONEY MARKET FUNDS IN JUL.</title>
<headline>TRIENA, ASPIS LEAD GREEK MONEY MARKET FUNDS IN JUL.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Triena and Aspis Pronia were leading Greece's 32 money market funds in July with year-to-date returns of 9.98 and 7.28 percent, respectively, the association of institutional investors said.</p>
<p>Money market funds under management reached 3.387 trillion drachmas in end-July, up 50.52 percent since the beginning of the year and 7.43 percent on June.</p>
<p>They made up 59.83 percent of the mutual fund industry's total assets which rose to 5.68 trillion drachmas, an increase of 4.93 percent on the previous month and 50.80 percent since the start of the year.</p>
<p>Greek money funds are required to invest a minimum of 65 percent of their assets in money market instruments.</p>
